Key Findings
Finding 1 — Seasonal Variation
- Historical sales show meaningful variation across the year, with July and Q3 among the stronger periods.
Finding 2 — Holiday Contribution
- Holiday-period sales account for approximately 7.5% of total revenue, highlighting the importance of holiday readiness.
Finding 3 — Revenue Concentration
- Sales are concentrated across higher-performing stores and departments, making performance prioritization important for operational planning.
Finding 4 — External Variables
- Temperature, fuel prices, CPI, unemployment and promotional variables were examined alongside sales. Their observed influence was generally less pronounced than recurring seasonal and operational patterns in this analysis.
Finding 5 — Forecasting Value
- Historical sales patterns provide useful signals for forward planning, particularly when combined with known seasonal periods.
Analytical Caution
- These are observational findings. They should not be interpreted as causal conclusions without additional statistical or experimental validation.
